{"name":"Pretty Peony","hex":"#ae5d6d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pretty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pleasant to the sight or other senses; attractive, especially of women or children. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Of objects or things: nice-looking, appealing."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Somewhat, fairly, quite; sometimes also (by meiosis) very.","Prettily, in a pretty manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pretty"},{"term":"peony","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flowering plant of the genus Paeonia with large fragrant flowers.","A dark red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peony"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peony","blocks":[{"text":"The peony or paeony is any flowering plant in the genus Paeonia, the only genus in the family Paeoniaceae. Peonies are native to Asia, Europe, and Western North America. Scientists differ on the number of species that can be distinguished, ranging from 25 to 40, although the current consensus describes 33 known species. The relationships between the species need to be further clarified."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/PaeoniaSuffruticosa7.jpg/330px-PaeoniaSuffruticosa7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peony","wikidata":"Q147105"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Paeonia-suffruticosa-buds.jpg/330px-Paeonia-suffruticosa-buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Paeonia-suffruticosa-buds.jpg/960px-Paeonia-suffruticosa-buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Paeonia-suffruticosa-buds.jpg/330px-Paeonia-suffruticosa-buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o